      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "With regard to total mortality rates, there is no benefit of primary prevention by lipid lowering. For the prevention of coronary events the use of statins seems to be effective in high risk individuals (risk of a coronary event > 3.0% per year) above a certain serum cholesterol level."},
